<!doctype html><html lang=en><meta charset=UTF-8><meta http-equiv=X-UA-Compatible content="IE=edge"><meta name=viewport content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Orgpedia: Information Extraction for Public Good</title><link rel=stylesheet href=c/output.css><link rel="shortcut icon" type=image/x-icon href=favicon.ico><body class=e-v><header><div class=a-c><div class=b-n><a href=index.html class=f-y><div class=b-g><p class=c-n><span class=text-blue-500>o</span>p</div><div class=b-y><img src=i/l-en.svg class=f-o alt="Orgpedia Logo"><p class=b-d>Information Extraction for Public Good</div></a><nav class=b-r><a href=projects.html class=e-d>Projects</a><a href=tracker.html class=e-d>Document Tracker</a><a href=en/ministry.html class=e-d>Council of Ministers</a><a href=annual_returns.html class=e-d>Annual Returns</a><a href=https://github.com/orgpedia target=_blank rel="noopener noreferrer" class=d-d><span>GitHub</span><img src=i/gh.svg class=g-d alt=GitHub></a></nav><div class=e-t><a href=projects.html class=c-g>Projects</a><a href=tracker.html class=c-o>Tracker</a></div></div></div></header><div class=b-w><div class=a-r><div class=f-f><span class=f-t>Home</span><span><img src=i/bc.svg class=g-d alt=">"></span><span class=g-g>About Orgpedia</span></div></div><section class=b-x><div class=c-x><div class=g-q><div class=b-a>Public Document Intelligence for India</div><h1 class=b-k>Making Public Governance Open, Legible & Actionable</h1><p class=c-y>Orgpedia enables citizens, researchers, journalists, and public administrators to understand the inner workings of Indian government institutions. We solve the hard computational problems of extracting, structuring, and verifying public knowledge from millions of opaque government orders, gazette notifications, and resolutions published across Indian languages.<p class=d-e>All extracted data, extraction code, and analysis tools are open-source. All information is presented in English and all<b>22 official Indian languages</b>recognized in the Eighth Schedule of the Indian Constitution.<div class=f-u><a href=projects.html class=a-o>Explore Projects &rarr;</a><a href=tracker.html class=a-f>View Data Tracker &rarr;</a><a href=#volunteer class=a-j>Volunteer with Us</a></div></div></div></section><section class=g-r><div class=b-l><div><h2 class=c-z>Document Intelligence Tracker</h2><p class=f-p>The end-to-end processing funnel from scanned government documents to consumable websites.</div><a href=tracker.html class=b-e>View Detailed Breakdown & Methodology &rarr;</a></div><div class=d-v><div class=a-e><div class=d-p><span class=c-i>Stage 1: Ingestion & OCR</span><span class=b-s>Raw Scans</span></div><div class=c-k>185,248</div><h3 class=d-q>Documents Processed</h3><p class=d-w>Total volume of government documents downloaded, organized and made available on Github, Huggingface and Archive.org.</div><div class=a-e><div class=d-p><span class=c-i>Stage 2: Extraction & Layout</span><span class=b-s>GovDoc Layers</span></div><div class=c-k>104,509</div><h3 class=d-q>Information Extracted</h3><p class=d-w>n Total volume of documents from which structured records and relevant entities are extracted and translated.</div><div class=a-e><div class=d-p><span class=c-i>Stage 3: Verification & Portals</span><span class=b-s>Public Access</span></div><div class=c-k>102,704</div><h3 class=d-q>Information Presented</h3><p class=d-w>Volume of documents whose entities are presented on websites.</div></div><div class=a-z>Want to see the breakup by department, language, and collection?<a href=tracker.html class=d-a>Explore the detailed data tracker page &rarr;</a></div></section><section class=g-r><div class=b-l><div><h2 class=c-z>Featured Projects</h2><p class=f-p>Explore interactive portals and open research tools developed by Orgpedia.</div><a href=projects.html class=b-e>View All Projects &rarr;</a></div><div class=d-x><div class=a-g><div><div class=e-r><img src=i/cover-pager-img.png alt="Parliament of India" class=c-m><div><div class=c-j>Flagship Portal</div><h3 class=e-i>Ministers of India</h3><p class=f-q>Central Cabinet Secretariat (1947–To Date)</div></div><p class=e-w>A comprehensive historical exploration of every minister, portfolio, and department in the Union Council of Ministers from Independence to the current 3rd Narendra Modi Ministry. Features interactive date filters, minister profiles, and full translation in 22 official Indian languages.</div><div class=b-z><span class=c-s>3,885+ Tenures &bull; 22 Languages</span><a href=en/ministry.html class=b-t>Open Council of Ministers &rarr;</a></div></div><div class=a-g><div><div class=e-r><img src=i/mantralay.png alt="Mantralaya Mumbai" class=c-m><div><div class=c-j>Weekly Monitor</div><h3 class=e-i>Weekly Summary of Maharashtra GRs</h3><p class=f-q>Government Resolutions Digest</div></div><p class=e-w>Automated tracking and digestible summarization of hundreds of Government Resolutions issued weekly by Maharashtra Mantralaya departments (Finance, Home, Urban Development, Public Health, and more).</div><div class=b-z><span class=c-s>Weekly Updates &bull; Multi-Dept</span><a href=https://mahsummary.orgpedia.in/en/index.html target=_blank rel="noopener noreferrer" class=b-t>View GR Summaries &rarr;</a></div></div></div></section><section id=volunteer class=b-v><div class=g-e><div class=b-b>Join the Mission</div><h2 class=c-z>Volunteer & Collaborate with Orgpedia</h2><p class=e-x>Orgpedia is an open-source, non-profit civic technology initiative. We are building digital public infrastructure for India, and we need your expertise.</div><div class=d-f><div class=c-w><div class=g-h>&#128483;</div><h3 class=d-z>Indic Language Reviewers</h3><p class=f-r>Help verify extracted names, designations, and tables in Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, Malayalam, Bengali, Gujarati, Odia, Punjabi, and other Eighth Schedule languages.</div><div class=c-w><div class=g-h>&#128187;</div><h3 class=d-z>Open Source Developers</h3><p class=f-r>Contribute to Python extraction pipelines, PDF geometry tools, Pydantic schemas, OCR/VLM benchmark harnesses, and interactive frontend data visualizations.</div><div class=c-w><div class=g-h>&#128269;</div><h3 class=d-z>Researchers & Journalists</h3><p class=f-r>Use our open datasets for investigative reporting, academic research into executive governance, or policy analysis on administrative postings.</div></div><div class=a-d><div><h4 class=e-j>Want to contribute your skills?</h4><p class=f-s>Reach out directly to our team with your language background or technical interests.</div><a href="mailto:info@orgpedia.in?subject=Volunteering with Orgpedia" class=a-h>Email info@orgpedia.in &rarr;</a></div></section><section class=c-p><div class=c-v><div class=g-q><h3 class=d-r>Governance & Non-Profit Credentials</h3><p class=d-g><b>Orgpedia Foundation</b>is a registered Section 8 (non-profit) company incorporated in Pune, Maharashtra, India. We are dedicated to transparency, public interest research, and open civic data infrastructure.<p class=f-r>To inspect our statutory filings, view the<a href=annual_returns.html class=d-a>Orgpedia Foundation Annual Returns</a>.</div><div class=b-m><h4 class=c-d>Developer Access</h4><p class=d-h>All extraction code, schemas, and public datasets are open source. Visit our GitHub organization to explore repositories, contribute, or download data.<div class=b-c><span>License: CC BY 4.0</span><a href=https://github.com/orgpedia target=_blank rel="noopener noreferrer" class=d-a>Visit GitHub &rarr;</a></div></div></div></section></div><footer><div class=c-l><div class=a-i><div class=f-g><img src=i/lf-en.svg alt="Orgpedia Logo" class=g-t><span>&bull;</span><a href=disclaimer.html class=g-b>Disclaimer</a><span>&bull;</span><a href=annual_returns.html class=g-b>Annual Returns</a><span>&bull;</span><a href="mailto:info@orgpedia.in?subject=Website Feedback" class=g-b>Report an Error</a></div><div class=f-h><div onclick="location.href='https://github.com/orgpedia';" style="cursor: pointer;" class=d-m><span>View on GitHub</span><img src=i/gh.svg class=g-p alt=GitHub></div><div class=f-i style="cursor: pointer;" onclick="location.href='https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/'"><img src=i/cc-1.svg class=g-u alt=CC> <img src=i/cc-2.svg class=g-u alt=BY></div></div></div></div><script defer=defer src=https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js data-cf-beacon='{"token": "4b28ac948b94411393435f9ff3e233ef"}'></script></footer>